About the role

OpenAI is seeking a technically rigorous, emotionally resilient Principal Institutional Balloon Restraint Engineer to help maintain contact between frontier-AI research and physical reality.

As model capabilities increase, ideas throughout the organisation can acquire unexpected buoyancy. A promising benchmark result may rise rapidly through several atmospheric layers, becoming first a product, then an industry, then a new economic system, and finally the machine-intelligence singularity—all before anyone has established who the customer is or whether the robot can stop when the Wi-Fi goes down.

You will identify these events early, trace the complete claim chain, locate missing assumptions and attach suitable restraints before the balloon enters public airspace.

This is not a pessimism role. We are not looking for somebody who walks around popping every ambitious idea with a pin.

We need somebody capable of determining:

* whether the balloon contains helium, hot air or a genuinely novel lifting mechanism;
* whether its stated destination follows from its current trajectory;
* whether the string is attached to anything;
* and whether management has accidentally valued the balloon as Amazon.

